{
  "configuration_id": "config_050",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies config_045 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.725 acc) as the best configuration, with every tested variation (avgpool, concat, resnet50, singleprofile) reducing accuracy. The remaining question is whether a cheaper combination of components (resnet50 + avgpool instead of imagenet_vit_l + transformer) can achieve comparable accuracy at lower cost, or whether the transformer aggregation and ViT-L image encoder are both essential for peak performance. Config_050 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) directly tests this: it keeps the proven scvi_n200 encoder and weighted fusion while swapping both the image encoder and aggregation to cheaper alternatives. If it lands near 0.71–0.72, it confirms config_045 is the accuracy winner; if it drops to ~0.69–0.70, it validates that the transformer+ViT-L combination is critical. This is the best use of experiment 8 because (1) no untested configuration is likely to beat 0.725, so the goal shifts to confirming the landscape and identifying cost-efficient alternatives, (2) it reduces uncertainty about which components drive the performance gap, and (3) with 2 experiments remaining, it preserves budget for a final confirmation run. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), cheaper than config_045 (3.60) and much cheaper than config_035 (6.22) due to avgpool replacing transformer and resnet50 replacing ViT-L."
}

